AionGuard component licensing

The custom license below is the project’s prospective licensing framework.
Its scope is defined by LICENSING-COVERAGE.json. Existing published code and
historical releases retain their valid MIT permissions, including commercial
use and redistribution. No existing published implementation is designated
as restricted by this update. No royalty debt is created for MIT users.

The original MIT license and copyright notice are preserved verbatim in
LICENSES/MIT-AionGuard-legacy.txt. Upstream Pinetree Research material and
third-party dependencies/assets retain their own terms and notices; see
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md. The cookbook root license is not changed.

Only future explicitly identified new material uses the custom terms below.
See COMMERCIAL-LICENSING.md and LICENSING-COVERAGE.json for the component
boundary and separate written commercial-permission process.

AionGuard Personal and Internal Business Use License 1.0

Prospective licensing framework adopted locally September 30, 2026.
This license applies only to Covered Material expressly identified below.
It does not replace previously granted MIT or third-party permissions.

1. Scope

"Covered Material" means copyrightable AionGuard material expressly marked
as subject to this license and identified by path and version/commit (or
baseline-plus-diff boundaries) in LICENSING-COVERAGE.json. "Licensors" means
its actual copyright holders or their authorized representatives. A person
may grant only rights they own or are authorized to grant. No unlisted
material is brought under this license by its presence in this repository.

Previously MIT-licensed material, Pinetree Research/Solari upstream material,
third-party dependencies, and separately licensed artwork/media retain their
applicable licenses. An entry for mixed material covers only the identified
new expression, not the MIT baseline. Valid MIT permissions remain available
for that baseline, including commercial use, distribution and sale. Nothing
here overrides another valid license the recipient holds for the same code.

2. Free permitted use

Subject to these conditions, Licensors grant a worldwide, nonexclusive,
no-charge copyright license to inspect, use, execute, copy and modify Covered
Material for personal use or Internal Business Use, and to distribute it
without compensation outside the commercial activities described in section 3.

"Internal Business Use" means use for an organization's own operations,
employees, authorized contractors and devices, including private deployments
on rented infrastructure. For-profit status alone does not require payment.
The organization may use findings and ordinary outputs in its business without
owing a share of unrelated revenue. A contractor may install, configure or
maintain that organization's internal deployment and charge for those services,
provided it does not sell software copies, bundle the software commercially,
or provide a paid hosted inspection service to external customers.

Gratis redistribution must preserve the copyright and license notices, this
license, the scope map and applicable third-party notices. Mark modifications
prominently. Recipients receive the permitted rights in original Covered
Material directly from its authorized Licensors. This does not assign the
modifier's copyright or require a copyright transfer. A distributor must
have and provide sufficient permissions for recipients to exercise these
permitted rights in the distributed copy; separately authored modifications
need not be licensed under identical terms. The restrictions on original
Covered Material remain applicable to copies or derivatives containing it.
Private modifications need not be published.

3. Separate commercial agreement

The free grant does not authorize:
(a) selling, reselling or distributing Covered Material, or a derivative
containing it, for compensation;
(b) hosting Covered Material to provide functionality to paying external
customers, including when access is part of a larger paid service; or
(c) including Covered Material, or a derivative containing it, in a commercial
product, appliance, client bundle or paid subscription offered to others.
A client supplied without a separate charge as part of a paid offering is
still commercial bundling.

Those activities require a separate written paid commercial agreement with
an authorized licensing representative before they begin. Fees or revenue
sharing, permitted versions/components and commercial rights are negotiated
in that agreement. This license specifies no royalty rate, automatic debt,
retroactive fee, or right to revenue from unrelated activities.

Ordinary paid cloud infrastructure used for an organization's internal
deployment is not a paid inspection offering by that organization. An operator
providing a managed hosted inspection service to paying external customers
falls under subsection (b), even when the customers use it internally.
Any special permission for trials, cost recovery, sponsored services or
other arrangements must be recorded in writing. This clause creates no
royalty merely because a user has sponsorship, advertising or donations;
resale, paid hosting and bundling are the permission triggers above.

4. Other rights and attribution

Preserve applicable prior MIT permissions and third-party license/NOTICE
files. This license imposes no new conditions on excluded material used alone
or in a larger distribution. It does not reserve facts, ideas, systems,
independently authored implementations, user data or ordinary findings/outputs.
Statutory exceptions and permissions obtained elsewhere are not displaced.
No copyright assignment is required by this license.

This license makes no express patent grant or determination of patent
ownership, validity, infringement or implied rights. Existing third-party
patent provisions retain their own effect. It grants no trademark, trade-name,
logo, endorsement or branding rights, including permission to use Solari,
Pinetree Research or the proposed SolariGuard name.

5. Conditions, breach and preservation

Permissions for Covered Material are conditional on compliance with this
license. A use outside the free grant requires the commercial agreement; it
does not become authorized by an assumed payment obligation. A breach does
not cancel independently granted MIT permissions or independent compliant
recipients' permissions. Licensors may grant separate written permissions.
No licensor can revoke third-party permissions by issuing a project notice.
The version of this license supplied with a copy governs that grant; a later
license edit does not silently impose new terms on that copy.

6. Warranty and liability

To the extent permitted by applicable law, Covered Material is provided AS IS,
without warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose,
title or noninfringement. To that extent, Licensors disclaim liability for
claims or damages arising from its use. Applicable mandatory law and any
express obligations in a separately signed agreement remain controlling.
No security, detection-accuracy or fitness guarantee is provided by the code
license. This text supplies no opinion on legal enforceability.
